      "reasoning": "Article 4 of Additional Protocol I expressly states that \"Neither the occupation of a territory nor the application of the Conventions and this Protocol shall affect the legal status of the territory in question.\" This provision demonstrates that the legal effect of the Conventions is independent of any question of who previously exercised sovereignty. Israel, as a High Contracting Party, therefore remains bound by the Fourth Geneva Convention in the occupied territories, even though Jordan’s title to the land was not universally recognised.",
