      "claim": "International criminal jurisdiction over alleged war crimes in the occupied Palestinian territories confirms that the Fourth Geneva Convention is deemed applicable to those areas.",
      "reasoning": "The Rome Statute gives the Court jurisdiction over \"grave breaches of the Geneva Conventions of 12 August 1949\" (Art. 8) and over \"serious violations of article 3 common to the four Geneva Conventions\" (Art. 8(2)(c)). By invoking these provisions in relation to conduct in the Palestinian territories, the Statute treats the Convention’s protections as operative there. The ICC’s practice in cases concerning the territories therefore substantiates the Convention’s applicability irrespective of the disputed sovereignty argument advanced by Israel.",
